course: dictionary
lesson: 916
title: Blank: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word blank has several meanings, so you must check the context to find the right one. «A new paragraph is shown by an indent or by a blank line» tells you blank means empty, with nothing written on it.
explain: Ask yourself what is missing. «Fill in the blanks» means fill in the empty spaces where missing words or numbers go. In «He gave me a blank look», the word shows no feeling, so the context points to a face with nothing showing in it.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If «my mind went blank» means you suddenly cannot remember anything, the sentence still makes sense. If your meaning does not fit, look for another meaning of blank.
fact: Blank means with nothing written, drawn or recorded on it, like a blank page or a blank screen.
fact: A blank is an empty space where you write a missing word or number.
fact: A blank look shows no feeling or understanding.
fact: If your mind goes blank, you suddenly cannot remember anything, which can happen when you feel nervous.
fact: Informally, to blank someone means to ignore them on purpose.
exercise: «Fill in the blanks: 5 + __ = 12.» What is a blank here? | A page with nothing on it | A gun with no bullet | *An empty space where you write a missing number
exercise: «Each people knew its own lands well, but far-off places were blank.» What does blank mean here? | Full of people and houses | *Nothing recorded, so not yet known or mapped | Painted bright white
exercise: «He gave me a blank look.» What does blank show? | Anger at once | Great joy | *No feeling or understanding
test: «Please fill in the blanks on the worksheet.» What are the blanks? | Long words to copy | Pictures of worksheets | *Empty spaces for missing words or numbers
test: In «My mind went blank in the test», what does blank mean? | I wrote a very long answer | I finished first and left the room | *I suddenly could not remember anything
exam: In «A blank is a gun cartridge with no bullet, which only makes a bang», what does blank mean? | A gun that never works | *Something with no real bullet inside | A loud noise that breaks glass | A gun made of paper
